# Chaos: damage number scatter (client/BASE.md 0081; after 0001-0080). The animated texts above the map (damage, healing, mana, experience) all rose on the same line, so an area hit or a group hunt stacked them into one unreadable column. AnimatedText gets a fixed pixel shift on top of the stacking offset (setScatter / getScatter) and a speed scale (setSpeedScale / getSpeedScale, clamped to 0.5 .. 2; 1 is the stock rise and fade of Otc::ANIMATED_TEXT_DURATION, 1.2 is 20% quicker): drawText uses the scaled duration for the rise, the sideways drift and the fade, and a text past its life is not drawn. The removal event checks the scaled life, so a slower text is not cut at the stock 1000 ms. Defaults (no shift, scale 1) draw exactly as before. No protocol change. The overlay module game_damagescatter calls them from g_map.onAnimatedText. C++ only.
